## Instructions

Produce your solution as the complete new contents of every file you change.
Requirements:

- For each file, output its repo-relative path on its own line, then one fenced
  code block holding the file's **entire** new contents:

      src/components/Cart/Cart.tsx
      ```tsx
      <the complete file, from its first line to its last>
      ```

- No prose before, between, or after the blocks.
- **Emit every line of the file, including the parts you did not change.** Never
  abbreviate with `// ...`, `// rest of the file unchanged`, `// existing code`,
  or any other placeholder. The block replaces the file wholesale, so anything
  you leave out is deleted.
- Only include files you actually change. Do not re-emit untouched files.
- To create a new file, give its path and its complete contents the same way.
- To delete a file, write `>>> DELETE <path>` on its own line.
- Keep the change itself minimal and focused on the task, even though the output
  is the whole file.
